  "id": "alternating-treatments-design",
  "term": "alternating treatments design",
  "definition": "An alternating treatments design is a single-subject research design used to compare the effects of different instructional approaches by applying them within the same study and tracking performance across sessions. In this packet, it refers to an adapted form used to evaluate which teaching method was more effective for specific learning skills.",
